{"name":"British Phone Booth","hex":"#ff0015","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"phone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A device for transmitting conversations and other sounds in real time across distances, now often a small portable unit also capable of running software etc.","A person's telephone number (as a means of contact); digits."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To call (someone) using a telephone.","To say via telephone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phone"},{"term":"booth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small stall for the display and sale of goods.","A temporary shelter, often in the form of a tent, shed, or canopied structure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/booth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Telephone booth","blocks":[{"text":"A telephone booth, phone booth, telephone kiosk, telephone call box, telephone box or public call box is a structure furnished with a payphone and designed for a telephone user's convenience; typically the user steps into the booth and closes the booth door while using the payphone inside."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Lightmatter_phonebooths_%28_South_Lake%2C_Pasadena%2C_California%29.jpg/330px-Lightmatter_phonebooths_%28_South_Lake%2C_Pasadena%2C_California%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telephone_booth"},{"title":"Telephone","blocks":[{"text":"A telephone, commonly shortened to phone, is a telecommunications device that enables two or more users to conduct a conversation when they are too far apart to be easily heard directly. A telephone converts sound, typically and most efficiently the human voice, into electronic signals that are transmitted via cables and other communication channels to another telephone which reproduces the sound to the receiving user. The term is derived from Ancient Greek: τῆλε, romanized: tēle, 